{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"9a3d0027739dfadbcc41b040","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1603"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1603: Reduce null agenda fields and escaped tag overhead in bounded context output"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"## Problem\n\n`pm context` is the first command an agent runs, and its brief depth runs under a 1,600-token budget. Two encodings in that budget carry no information:\n\n1. **Null event fields on every agenda entry.** A plain deadline entry prints 8 `event_*` keys that only calendar events use, all `null`:\n\n   ```\n   events[1]:\n     - at: \"2026-11-01T00:00:00.000Z\"\n       date: 2026-11-01\n       kind: deadline\n       reminder_text: null\n       event_title: null\n       event_end: null\n       event_location: null\n       event_all_day: null\n       event_timezone: null\n       event_recurring: null\n       event_recurrence_rule: null\n       item_id: ...\n   ```\n\n   That is about 200 bytes per deadline or reminder. A tracker with 10 upcoming deadlines spends about 2 KB of a 6.4 KB brief response on nulls.\n\n2. **Tags as backslash-escaped JSON inside tabular rows.** `high_level[]` declares `json_columns: [tags]`, and each row then carries `\"[\\\"automation\\\",\\\"ci\\\",\\\"fleet\\\",\\\"release\\\"]\"`. On a real 1,300-item tracker, one `pm context --limit 10` response held 74 `\\\"` escapes, about 3% of the output, and agents have to unescape twice to read the tags.\n\n## Repro (pm-cli 2026.10.26)\n\n```bash\npm create --type Chore --title \"deadline probe\" --deadline 2026-11-01\npm context --limit 10 | grep -A12 '^  events'\npm context --limit 10 | grep -o '\\\\\"' | wc -l\n```\n\n## Proposal\n\n- Agenda entries omit `event_*` keys whose value is null (or only emit them for `kind: event`), at least at `brief` and `standard` depth. `--format json` and `--depth full` can keep the full shape for schema-stable consumers.\n- Tabular array columns use a delimiter-joined scalar that needs no escaping, declared once in the encoding header (e.g. `list_columns: {tags: \";\"}` → `automation;ci;fleet;release`). Tag values that contain the delimiter would fall back to the current JSON form.\n\nBoth changes keep the projection lossless and shrink the response that every agent session starts with.\n\n\nImplementation boundary: reproduce against the published and current hosts in an isolated tracker. Preserve SDK and full JSON data semantics, tabular codec round trips, receipts and output-budget accounting. Evaluate compact list encoding with explicit metadata and an unambiguous fallback; a delimiter proposal is not an accepted wire contract. Completed agenda deduplication and lossless JSON fixes remain delivered."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context","github","output","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Native isolated deadline/reminder/event fixtures measure the actual byte and token reduction at brief and standard depth without weakening full JSON or SDK facts.; Tags round-trip through declared compact encoding with empty arrays, delimiters, commas, quotes, escapes, newlines and Unicode; ambiguous inputs retain a lossless fallback.; Serializer-aware whole-envelope budgets, omission receipts and CLI/MCP/SDK parity remain executable and unchanged."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-mpbb"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"Brief and standard context output spend their budget on useful facts while full JSON and published SDK contracts preserve exact null, empty, tag and calendar facts."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-4euctr","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-5y05kq","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"},{"id":"pm-6m1i","kind":"related","created_at":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z","author":"harness:codex","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-26T15:33:34.776Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Duplicate check: fresh measured orientation, request-specific agenda and TOON searches, open and in-progress inventories, and complete strict 3125-item all-status corpus found no open owner for this exact proposal. Full live data and histories confirm pm-6m1i, pm-4euctr and pm-5y05kq are completed related work; keep them closed. GH1603 arrived during PR1596 validation and is intake only, open and unclaimed."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"f66c538b639f0bbbfd3094e58d0937b6a7f17240c0b7005e3aa5d9e618d0bd64","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex